      "disposition": "STILL_UNRESOLVED",
      "why": "The regulatory definition of a Category A ship (IMO‑001 §2.1) requires that the ship be designed for operation in polar waters. The supplied SHACL shape validates the shipCategory and designIceCondition, but it never asserts or constrains the ship's operational region (e.g., using the property nltl:shipOperatesInPolarWaters). Without this constraint the shape cannot enforce the full regulatory obligation, leaving a material gap.",
